ne season, Beryl broke many meteorological records for the months of June and July, primarily for formation and intensity.","extract_html":"<p><b>Hurricane Beryl</b> was a deadly and destructive tropical cyclone that impacted parts of the Caribbean, the Yucatán Peninsula, and the Gulf Coast of the United States in late June and early July 2024. It was the earliest-forming Category 5 hurricane on record and the second such storm in the month of July, the other being 2005's Hurricane Emily. Beryl was also the strongest hurricane to develop within the Main Development Region (MDR) of the Atlantic before the month of July. The second named storm, first hurricane, and first major hurricane of the 2024 Atlantic hurricane season, Beryl <span class=\"mw-selflink-fragment\">broke many meteorological records</span> for the months of June and July, primarily for formation and intensity.</p>"}